It moves about (instead of being stationary) ;
The skin above it becomes thin or attenuated ;
It presents a rough exterior, and in colour it becomes either red or dark ;
Loss of sensation (as regards the exterior surface), erection of the hair that grows on the part afflicted, and (internal) pain.
Disappearance (or alleviation) without apparent cause.
It goes down when pressed (and rises up when the pressure is withdrawn).
Its strength is manifested during the daytime. 10

It is mild (_i. e._, soft), and has a smell of its own ;
In colour it is either dark, or yellow, or red ;
It is accompanied by vertigo, fever, perspiration, thirst, and a sense of inebriation ;
It has great heat, and produces pain if touched ;
It causes the eyes to become red ;
It is accompanied by a burning sensation, and ends in suppuration. 11
